<section class="placeholder-text container">
  <p>
    Eden Ben-Shoshan ’28, the executive vice president of the Residence Hall Council (RHC), said in an interview with The Herald that her biggest advice is to “go in with a plan” and “know who you want to live with.” She joined the RHC because she “felt it would have been nice to have someone that could advocate for (her)”—someone living in the dorms that could “propose solutions to common problems.”
  </p>
  <p>
    “Start touring dorms,” Ben-Shoshan said, highlighting tours held by the Office of Residential Life—also known as ResLife—as a key source of information. “You can actually go into people’s dorms and see, what does it look like? How big is it? What do the bathrooms look like? Where’s the laundry room? I think that was a really great way for me to inform where I might want to live and to see where the location is on campus.”
  </p>
  <p>
    Along with the above map, The Herald also created a graph highlighting overall housing availability, with students able to toggle room types and sizes accordingly. This will also update in real-time as rooms get selected during this year’s housing selection days.
  </p>
</section>

